Vulkan: nriConvertVKFormatToNRI maps the block-compressed VkFormats.

VKFormatToNRIFormat looks a VkFormat up in VK_FORMAT_TABLE, which ends at
VK_FORMAT_D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT (130), and special-cases four formats past the end (the two-plane
YUV formats and A4R4G4B4). VkFormat 131 to 184 are BC1 to BC7, ETC2/EAC and ASTC LDR. NRI has
every one of them as a Format, and NRIFormatToVKFormat (g_Formats in ConversionVK.hpp) produces
them, but the forward conversion returns Format::UNKNOWN for all 52 that NRI names. A texture
imported with CreateTextureVK, or a format read back from a VkImage created elsewhere, can
therefore not be described in NRI terms, and NRI -> VK -> NRI is not an identity for any
compressed format (measured on v190 through nriConvertNRIFormatToVK / nriConvertVKFormatToNRI).

This extends the table to 184 with one entry per VkFormat, in the table's existing style. The
two BC1 RGB formats (131, 132) stay UNKNOWN: NRI has only the RGBA variants and g_Formats never
produces the RGB ones. Every other entry is the exact inverse of g_Formats. Nothing else changes.

Applies on top of NRI v190, independent of the other patches.

